          }
        ]
      },
      "note": [
        "The table contains data on urban population with public green areas within 200, 300 and 500 meters from place of permanent residence. The urban population is disaggregated by sex and age. A public green area is defined as an area of contiguous green space of at least 0.5 hectares, which is available for the public. Place of permanent residence is defined by the coordinates of the address location to which an individual is registered. Distance is calculated as the Euclidian distance between dwelling and public green areas without regard to physical barriers such as water or major roads and railways. Shares refer to the share of the population within each group with public green areas within respective distances from dwelling."
      ],
